      "body": "Some cameras only have a USB-C port, rather than the Multi accessory port.\n\nThe serial bootloader might work there too, if someone can figure out the pinout. It might be the USB-C SBU pins - you could test with a breakout like this\n\n<img width=\"512\" height=\"387\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2b6e0eea-8832-458b-a8dc-ae113abd2844\" />\n\nIt may also be multiplexed over one of the other pins, conditional on the CC lines being pulled one way or another e.g. DAM mode\n\nTest with [uart_boot_probe.ino](https://github.com/DavidBuchanan314/ILCE-7M4-RE/blob/main/tools/uart_boot_probe/uart_boot_probe.ino) initially, because it should still work even if RST isn't connected, you only need to find RX. (It doesn't matter who drives the reset, it just matters that the waveform is present during early boot. for example, you could start the waveform and then insert the battery to trigger a fresh boot.)",
