      "body": "Hi David, thanks for sharing this project!\n\nI'm trying to understand how to reproduce the setup shown in your [Multi-port breakout photo](https://github.com/DavidBuchanan314/ILCE-7M4-RE/blob/main/images/multi_breakout.jpg):\n\n![Multi-port breakout and RP2040](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DavidBuchanan314/ILCE-7M4-RE/main/images/multi_breakout.jpg)\n\nIn `tools/uart_boot/uart_boot.ino`, I see `MULTI_TX = 28`, `MULTI_RX = 29`, and `MULTI_RST = 27`, and the Makefile targets a Waveshare RP2040-Zero. However, I can't determine the exact connector pin mapping from the photo.\n\nCould you share a wiring diagram or pin-to-pin table covering:\n\n1. Which Sony Multi connector contacts connect to RP2040 GPIO 28, 29, 27, and GND? Please include the connector viewing orientation so the pin numbering is unambiguous.\n2. How are the USB cable's D+, D-, VBUS, and GND wired to the breakout? Is that cable connected directly to the computer for the camera's fastboot connection, while a separate USB cable connects the RP2040-Zero to the computer? How should VBUS/power be handled?\n3. With the default `OPEN_DRAIN` build, are any external resistors or level shifters required? What are the camera-side signal voltages? I also noticed the comment that enabling `UART_TX` requires a level shifter.\n4. What Multi connector/breakout part did you use, and is there a part number or supplier link?\n\nMy camera is an ILCE-7M4 running stock firmware V6.02. I'd like to confirm the wiring before connecting the bridge.\n\nThanks!",
